# Every environment variable UniversityFlow reads is documented here. Copy to `.env` for local
# development. Never commit `.env`.

# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Postgres (`pnpm db:up` starts one in Docker) or embedded Postgres with no setup at all:
#   DATABASE_URL=pglite:./.data/pglite
# Production is RDS in af-south-1 (Cape Town) and must be a postgres:// URL.
# The judge demo ONLY (made-up learners) may use Supabase: its TRANSACTION pooler string,
#   postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?sslmode=verify-full
# with DATABASE_CA_CERT below (docs/deploy/demo.md). Real learners' data never goes there: it stays
# in South Africa (RDS af-south-1, a locked decision). Every server instance migrates the database
# as it starts, safely when several start at once, through a transaction pooler too: no second
# "direct" URL is needed. A demo refuses a Postgres across the internet without TLS.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://universityflow:universityflow@localhost:5432/universityflow

# Optional: the PEM certificate the database server's must chain to (Supabase: Database settings
# → SSL configuration → Download certificate; Node does not trust Supabase's own root CA). Set, the
# server is always verified against it, hostname included, whatever DATABASE_URL's sslmode says.
# Paste the whole file; on one line, write \n for each line break.
# DATABASE_CA_CERT=-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\n…\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----

# Never read as the database: Vercel's Supabase integration sets these (and SUPABASE_* keys), not
# DATABASE_URL. A demo with any of them and no DATABASE_URL refuses to start, rather than quietly
# fall back to an embedded database per instance. Don't install the integration; set DATABASE_URL.
# POSTGRES_URL=
# POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL=
# POSTGRES_URL_NON_POOLING=

# Optional: a scratch Postgres for the database tests that also run on the real driver.
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://universityflow:universityflow@localhost:5432/universityflow

# ── Security ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keys one-time-PIN hashes. At least 32 random characters; required in production.
# Generate one: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
AUTH_SECRET=

# ── Providers (decision D8) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `local` runs everything against stand-ins: SMS to an in-memory outbox (/dev/outbox), files to
# UF_FILE_STORE_DIR, scheduled jobs to a table in DATABASE_URL, and a scripted AI unless
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set. `live` uses S3, the SMS provider UF_SMS_PROVIDER names, the job
# scheduler UF_JOBS_PROVIDER names, and Claude, and refuses to start if any of them is missing; it
# never falls back to a stand-in. Production refuses `local`. A judge demo (UF_DEPLOYMENT=demo)
# whose DATABASE_URL is Postgres keeps its files in that database instead of UF_FILE_STORE_DIR
# (docs/deploy/demo.md); nothing to set.
UF_PROVIDERS=local
UF_FILE_STORE_DIR=./.data/files

# ── Live file storage: S3 (UF_PROVIDERS=live) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# A private bucket in af-south-1 (planning.md §16.1): Block Public Access on, no public ACLs.
# Every object is encrypted (SSE-S3, or SSE-KMS with UF_S3_KMS_KEY_ID). Browsers upload straight
# to the bucket with short-lived signed forms, so the bucket needs a CORS rule allowing POST from
# UF_PUBLIC_URL, and a lifecycle rule expiring "<prefix>incoming-" objects after a day.
# Credentials come from the AWS SDK's default chain (the deployment's role, or the standard
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY / AWS_SESSION_TOKEN); the app never reads them itself.
# Also set at build time: the bucket's address goes into the Content-Security-Policy.
# Required in live mode. Lower-case letters, digits and hyphens (no dots).
# UF_S3_BUCKET=
# Default af-south-1; production refuses any other region (student data stays in South Africa).
# UF_S3_REGION=af-south-1
# Optional: a KMS key id or ARN for SSE-KMS. Unset means S3-managed keys (SSE-S3).
# UF_S3_KMS_KEY_ID=
# Folder inside the bucket. Default documents/
# UF_S3_PREFIX=documents/
# Local testing only: an S3-compatible server instead of AWS. Production refuses it.
# UF_S3_ENDPOINT=

# ── Live SMS (UF_PROVIDERS=live) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The SMS provider's adapter name (apps/web/lib/server/sms-providers.ts). Required in live mode.
# The adapter must send and receive (A5-02): its inbound verifier hears STOP, replies and delivery
# reports at /api/messaging/sms/inbound, where the provider's webhooks point.
# No adapter exists until the owner chooses the provider, so live mode refuses to start for now.
# UF_SMS_PROVIDER=
# Global SMS budgets (open finding 1), across every number and every server, counted in billed
# SMS segments (A1-14: a PIN is 1, a guardian link 2, a reminder 1 or 2). Sending stops (fails
# closed) when either rolling window is spent, with a log line at 80% and at 100% per budget.
# Two budgets (A5-01), so reminders can never lock anyone out of sign-in. All four defaults are
# placeholders until the owner sets them from the provider's pricing.
# Sign-in PINs and guardian consent links ("sms-auth"). Defaults 300 an hour and 2000 a day.
# UF_SMS_BUDGET_PER_HOUR=300
# UF_SMS_BUDGET_PER_DAY=2000
# Reminders ("sms-reminders"). A reminder it refuses waits for the window to pass, then tries
# again. Defaults 1000 an hour and 4000 a day.
# UF_SMS_REMINDER_BUDGET_PER_HOUR=1000
# UF_SMS_REMINDER_BUDGET_PER_DAY=4000
# WhatsApp ("whatsapp", A12-15): Meta bills every template message, so WhatsApp has a global
# budget too, one unit a template message; replies inside the learner's 24-hour window are free
# and not counted. Same windows, same 80%/100% log lines, and a reminder it refuses waits for the
# window to pass. Defaults 500 an hour and 2000 a day: placeholders until the owner sets them
# from Meta's pricing.
# UF_WHATSAPP_BUDGET_PER_HOUR=500
# UF_WHATSAPP_BUDGET_PER_DAY=2000

# ── Store-review sign-in (audit A7-01, docs/store/review-notes.md option A) ─────────────────
# App Store and Play reviewers sign in to one synthetic adult account with a fixed PIN. Off
# unless all three are set; any one without the others refuses to start. Set them in Vercel
# (Production) only for a submission's review window, and remove them after. Works with
# UF_PROVIDERS=live; it is not a stand-in. Requesting a PIN for this number sends no SMS and
# spends no SMS budget; every sign-in writes an audit row and a "store-review sign-in" log line.
# The number: a company SIM the owner keeps for this, never a person's.
# UF_REVIEW_PHONE=
# The PIN's hash, never the PIN: 64 lower-case hex digits, HMAC-SHA256 under AUTH_SECRET of
# "<number as +27…>:<six-digit PIN>". Re-make it if AUTH_SECRET changes. The one-line command is
# in docs/store/review-notes.md. Ten wrong review PINs in a window lock the review sign-in until
# a new hash (or date) is set.
# UF_REVIEW_PIN_HASH=
# The last day the PIN works (YYYY-MM-DD, to the end of that day, South African time), at most
# 31 days away. Required: the review sign-in always expires.
# UF_REVIEW_UNTIL=

# ── Messaging: WhatsApp, push and inbound webhooks (Phase 4a) ───────────────────────────────
# Signs the stand-in channels' inbound webhooks (/api/messaging/sms/inbound and
# /api/messaging/whatsapp/inbound: STOP, replies, delivery reports): header
# `x-uf-signature: t=<unix seconds>,v1=<hex HMAC-SHA256 of "<t>.<channel>.<body>">`, the body
# being the event as JSON plus an optional `id` (the provider's message id). A forged, unsigned,
# stale or replayed request, or one signed for the other channel, is refused (A5-06). At least
# 32 random characters. Unset locally, a development default is used. In live mode these routes
# use each live adapter's own verifier instead (A5-02), and this secret is not used.
# UF_MESSAGING_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Live WhatsApp and push adapters (apps/web/lib/server/messaging-providers.ts). Optional in live
# mode: unset, the channel is simply not offered; named without an adapter, live mode refuses to
# start. A WhatsApp adapter (like an SMS one) must also receive, or live mode refuses to start:
# point the provider's webhooks at /api/messaging/whatsapp/inbound. No WhatsApp adapter exists
# until the owner chooses the provider.
# UF_WHATSAPP_PROVIDER=
# Push: `expo` sends through Expo's push service (https://exp.host), which hands notifications to
# Apple and Google, outside South Africa: notifications carry no personal data for that reason
# (docs/audits/A11-privacy-popia.md). Delivery receipts are checked by the `receipt.check` job
# about 15 minutes after each send.
# UF_PUSH_PROVIDER=expo
# Required with UF_PUSH_PROVIDER=expo (A5-03, A11-06): an Expo access token, with "Enhanced
# security for push notifications" turned on for the project at expo.dev
# (docs/store/release-checklist.md). Without it anyone holding a learner's push token could push
# any text to their phone, so live mode refuses to start. A secret: set it in Vercel, never in a
# file. Not needed locally (the push stand-in).
# EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# ── Live scheduled jobs (UF_PROVIDERS=live) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The job scheduler's adapter name (apps/web/lib/server/job-providers.ts). Required in live mode.
# No adapter exists until the owner connects the hosted scheduler (spike 5), so live mode refuses
# to start for now rather than use the local Postgres queue.
# UF_JOBS_PROVIDER=

# Optional: a scratch S3-compatible server for the storage tests that also run against real S3
# (packages/documents). For example a throwaway SeaweedFS container:
#   docker run -d --name uf-s3-test -p 127.0.0.1:55491:8333 \
#     -e AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=uftest -e AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=uftest-secret-key \
#     -e WEED_S3_SSE_KEY=<base64 of 32 random bytes> -e WEED_JWT_FILER_SIGNING_KEY=<random hex> \
#     chrislusf/seaweedfs server -s3 -dir=/data
# TEST_S3_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:55491
# TEST_S3_BUCKET=uf-test
# TEST_S3_REGION=af-south-1
# TEST_S3_ACCESS_KEY=uftest
# TEST_S3_SECRET_KEY=uftest-secret-key

# Show catalogue records that are researched but not yet verified, labelled as such. For local
# development and E2E only: production refuses it (hard rule 3).
UF_CATALOGUE_PREVIEW=1

# Add the synthetic draft records the E2E journeys need (apps/web/lib/server/e2e-fixtures.ts: a
# TEST-coded first-year curriculum for the registration check). E2E only; production refuses it.
# UF_CATALOGUE_E2E_FIXTURES=1

# The profile photo on About me (docs/design/profile-look-proposal.md §5.3), for learners from
# Grade 10, used for nothing else (docs/deploy/profile-photo.md). Production refuses it until the
# live consent wording names the photo (guardian v4 and adult-v3, legal review; A11-31); from then
# on, setting it is the one switch-on step. Before then it is the owner's preview, standing in for
# the wording in the database (migration 0037). A staging site always refuses it. Off (the
# default), /api/me/photo answers 404 (but "Remove photo") and neither the web nor the app offers one.
# UF_PROFILE_PHOTO=1

# My plan maps: let learners write their own words in a map (a title, each part's words, what got
# in the way, what to try differently). Off by default: no consent wording names plan maps yet
# (guardian v4 and adult-v3 are owed legal review), so without it learners choose a template and
# tick parts only, and the database refuses the words. On in the owner's preview only, and on a
# judge demo (a hackathon exception, 2026-10-24: docs/deploy/hackathon-undo-pr.md); production
# and a staging site refuse it. The crisis check reads every save.
# UF_MINDMAP_WORDS=1

# My CV, made by Mmereko as our operator (docs/design/mmereko-api-proposal.md). Off by default:
# no live consent wording names Mmereko yet (guardian v4 and adult-v3, owed legal review), so it
# is the owner's preview only, on the in-memory stand-in engine; production and a staging site
# refuse it. A judge demo may switch it on with the stand-in only (a hackathon exception,
# 2026-10-24): it refuses UF_CV_PROVIDER and every MMEREKO_* (D14). Off, every CV route answers 404.
# UF_CV=1
# The live CV engine, once the wording names Mmereko: an adapter in apps/web/lib/server/
# cv-providers.ts (none yet: Mmereko's joins after its sandbox passes the contract). Unset: the
# stand-in. Needs UF_CV=1.
# UF_CV_PROVIDER=mmereko
# Mmereko's partner API (OAuth 2.0 client credentials, §4.1): the base URL (https, ending in
# /partner/v1), our client id and secret, and the webhook secret it signs with (at least 32
# characters each). The _NEXT secrets carry a rotation: both are accepted until the old one goes.
# MMEREKO_API_URL=https://partner.mmereko.example/partner/v1
# MMEREKO_CLIENT_ID=
# MMEREKO_CLIENT_SECRET=
# MMEREKO_CLIENT_SECRET_NEXT=
# MMEREKO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# MMEREKO_WEBHOOK_SECRET_NEXT=
# Where Mmereko's partner cell runs. Production (and any live run) refuses Mmereko unless this is
# exactly af-south-1 (Cape Town): learners' CV data stays in South Africa (D3, POPIA s72, A11-35).
# Set it only once Mmereko confirms in writing that the partner cell runs there.
# MMEREKO_REGION=af-south-1
# Tests only: run the CV engine contract against Mmereko's sandbox (apps/web/test/
# mmereko-sandbox.test.ts; synthetic data only; never in CI by default), with the sandbox's own
# MMEREKO_* values. The adapter joins CV_ADAPTERS only once this passes.
# UF_MMEREKO_SANDBOX_CONTRACT=1
# "Open Mmereko" on My CV (the owner's decision of 2026-10-24): a button on /cv that opens
# Mmereko's own site in a full-screen canvas, for a learner 18 or over (by their confirmed date of
# birth) or at university; never an under-18 school learner. Off by default; needs UF_CV=1. It is
# a separate service with its own account: UniversityFlow sends it nothing (no query, no message),
# and the privacy page says so. Only /cv's CSP may frame it, and only with this on. Not a partner
# setting, so unlike the MMEREKO_* above a judge demo and production may carry it (production only
# once UF_CV may). docs/deploy/production.md, docs/deploy/demo.md.
# UF_CV_MMEREKO_CANVAS=1
# Mmereko's site, an https origin alone (no path or query). Unset: https://mmereko.tumoolo.tech.
# The canvas opens <origin>/login and links <origin>/ (Mmereko has no privacy page yet).
# MMEREKO_APP_URL=https://mmereko.tumoolo.tech

# Where links in SMS messages (the guardian consent link) point. Production refuses to start
# without its own plain https address here (no path, query or localhost; A1-50).
UF_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Local debugging only: print full server errors. Never on the deployed site (hard rule 4).
# UF_DEBUG_ERRORS=1

# Any production build counts as production and refuses the stand-ins above. Set this only for
# a production build run on this machine (the E2E tests do); it is ignored on Vercel.
# UF_LOCAL_PRODUCTION_BUILD=1

# ── Deployment (docs/deploy/README.md) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset: production (Vercel, cpt1, live providers). `staging`: a test copy on synthetic data
# only, as render.yaml sets up on Render. Staging refuses UF_PROVIDERS=live and Vercel
# production, needs a long AUTH_SECRET, shows a "Staging" banner on every page and is never
# indexed. Any other value refuses to start. Staging also refuses real data and keys (A5-11):
# a DATABASE_URL that isn't pglite:, any UF_S3_*, AWS credentials, an AI, voice or push key,
# the webhook secret, any live provider and the store-review sign-in.
# UF_DEPLOYMENT=staging

# Staging only: the access gate's password (A5-10). Every page and API route of a staging site
# asks for it (HTTP Basic, any user name); only /api/health is open, for the host's probe.
# At least 16 characters; a staging site refuses to start without it. Set it in the host's
# dashboard and share it only with testers; never commit it.
# UF_STAGING_PASSWORD=

# ── Judge demo mode (docs/deploy/demo.md) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `UF_DEPLOYMENT=demo`: a public demo on made-up learners only, in its OWN Vercel project (never
# production's). No phone sign-in (request-pin, verify-pin, /dev/outbox and guardian SMS answer
# 404); `/` and `/sign-in` show "Try UniversityFlow as…" with six made-up learners; each visit gets
# its own copy, deleted after 24 hours; uploads take only the results generator's SAMPLE PDFs.
# A demo refuses UF_PROVIDERS=live and everything production is made of: any UF_S3_*, AWS
# credentials, SMS/WhatsApp/push/jobs providers, EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN, UF_ELEVENLABS_MINORS_APPROVED,
# Mmereko (UF_CV_PROVIDER, MMEREKO_*), the store-review sign-in, the webhook secret,
# UF_PROFILE_PHOTO, UF_STAGING_PASSWORD and UF_CATALOGUE_E2E_FIXTURES. Hackathon exceptions of
# 2026-10-24 (docs/deploy/hackathon-undo-pr.md): it allows UF_CV=1 (My CV on the stand-in),
# UF_MINDMAP_WORDS=1 and ElevenLabs' key and voice (Read aloud). It needs a long AUTH_SECRET. It allows
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and GEMINI_API_KEY (the real AI) and UF_CATALOGUE_PREVIEW=1 (drafts, labelled).
# UF_DEPLOYMENT=demo
#
# Demo only, required there: says this is the demo's own project. Production and staging refuse
# every UF_DEMO_* variable, so a demo setting copied by mistake stops them starting.
# UF_DEMO_PROJECT=1
#
# Demo only: a Postgres DATABASE_URL is accepted only with this set, meaning "a database made for
# the demo, holding made-up learners only" (the Supabase project made for it). Without it, a demo
# needs DATABASE_URL=pglite:… (or, on Vercel with none set, the embedded one in /tmp, which each
# function instance keeps separately: use the Postgres for anything judges touch).
# UF_DEMO_DATABASE=synthetic
#
# Demo only, optional: AI chat messages a day across the whole demo. Unset or empty: no cap (the
# owner's choice: judges are never cut off). Over it, a kind line and the scripted stand-in
# replies. Either way, set a monthly spend limit on each AI key in the provider's console.
# UF_DEMO_AI_DAILY_CAP=
#
# Demo only, optional: 1 shows the universities' own logos beside their names, with a "for this
# demo only, not affiliated" line in the banner (the owner's decision of 2026-10-23, for the FNB
# hackathon only; apps/web/lib/demo-logos.ts). Read at BUILD time: redeploy after changing it.
# Production and staging refuse it. Remove after the hackathon.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_UF_DEMO_LOGOS=1
#
# Demo only, optional: 1 lets a visitor upload their OWN profile photo beside the six drawn
# samples, a HACKATHON EXCEPTION (the owner's decision of 2026-10-23, late night; docs/deploy/demo.md
# "Hackathon exceptions"). Kept only in their demo copy (the demo's Postgres when it has one) and
# deleted with it; used for nothing else; the usual limits apply. Production and staging refuse it.
# Remove after the hackathon (docs/deploy/hackathon-undo-pr.md, D).
# UF_DEMO_REAL_PHOTOS=1
#
# Demo only, optional: `onscreen` lets judges sign up as a NEW LEARNER the real way (number, PIN,
# date of birth, consent, onboarding) on made-up details, a HACKATHON EXCEPTION (the owner's
# decision of 2026-10-24; docs/deploy/demo.md "Hackathon exceptions"). Only made-up toll-free
# numbers (080…) are taken, never a cellphone, for the learner and for a minor's guardian. NOTHING
# IS SENT: the PIN, and the guardian's consent link, are shown on screen. Every such account is
# deleted 24 hours after it was made (the demo's sweep). Unset: phone sign-in answers 404 on the
# demo, as before. Production and staging refuse it. Remove after the hackathon
# (docs/deploy/hackathon-undo-pr.md, H).
# UF_DEMO_PHONE_SIGNUP=onscreen
#
# Demo only, optional: the judges' real sign-up, a HACKATHON EXCEPTION (the owner's approval of
# 2026-10-23; docs/deploy/demo.md "Hackathon exceptions"; undo after the hackathon). Off unless
# set: without it the demo is exactly as above. `firebase` lets an adult judge sign in with
# Firebase Authentication (email link or Google; adults only; deleted 30 days after sign-up), and
# needs the three NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_* values below. `fake` is a stand-in for this machine only
# (the demo E2E), refused on a host. Production and staging refuse all four.
# UF_DEMO_SIGNUP=firebase
# The Firebase project's web app config (Project settings → Your apps → Web). Public values, read
# on the server and handed to the sign-up page only.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=<project>.firebaseapp.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
#
# Demo only, optional: the main site's address, for "Back to UniversityFlow" in the demo banner
# (an https URL). Unset: the demo's own landing page.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_UF_MAIN_URL=https://<the main site>
#
# Demo only: the secret behind the demo's SCHEDULED sweep (A11-61; docs/deploy/demo.md "The
# scheduled sweep"; a hackathon exception, docs/deploy/hackathon-undo-pr.md M). Vercel's own name:
# with it set in the project, Vercel sends `Authorization: Bearer <value>` when its cron
# (apps/web/vercel.json) calls GET /api/demo/sweep, which deletes made-up learners' copies after
# 24 hours, the judges' sign-up accounts after 30 days, queued files, and expired sessions, even
# when nobody visits. At least 32 random characters (a demo refuses a shorter one); unset, the
# route answers 503 and logs why, and only the lazy sweep runs. Mark it Sensitive in Vercel.
# Production and staging refuse it like every demo switch. Remove after the hackathon.
# CRON_SECRET=

# Optional, any deployment: the judge demo's address (an https URL). Set, the landing page shows
# "Demo for judges", a plain link to it (no session or data goes across). Unset: no link.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_UF_DEMO_URL=https://universityflow.vercel.app

# Set by Render to `true` on every service; never set it yourself. Production refuses to start
# where it is set: Render has no South African region, so student data never goes there.
# RENDER=true

# ── AI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# With a key, the chat and report reading use Claude; without one, the scripted stand-ins.
# Required in live mode.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# The model, as decided in planning.md §16.3.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5
# Which provider the chat asks first: anthropic (the default) or gemini (owner's decision of
# 2026-10-23, the judge demo first). Production refuses gemini, and refuses GEMINI_API_KEY too,
# until the consent wording, the privacy page and legal review name Google as an operator.
# Reading documents stays with Anthropic either way. With both keys set, the other provider
# answers a message the chosen one can't (network, server error, rate limit). No key for either:
# the scripted stand-in (locally).
UF_AI_PROVIDER=anthropic
# Google's Gemini API key. Never on staging (A5-11), never in production; allowed on a judge demo
# (docs/deploy/demo.md), with a monthly spend limit set on it in Google's console. Read only where the
# chat model is made (lib/server/chat-model.ts), never kept in the configuration.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Gemini's model id; the default is the stable one Google recommends (packages/agent gemini-model.ts).
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash

# ── Read aloud: ElevenLabs (owner's choice of 2026-10-22) ──────────────────────────────────
# Read aloud speaks only in this ElevenLabs voice, on the web and in the app (or through the
# learner's own screen reader in the app). With no key, there is no Read aloud button at all:
# never a browser or phone voice instead. The key stays on the server; the browser and the app
# ask /api/speech/<place id>, and only public campus text is ever sent to ElevenLabs.
# Live, setting any of these without both the key and the voice refuses to start.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# The voice's id, from the ElevenLabs voice library. Required with the key.
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=
# Optional: the model. Unset, ElevenLabs' default, eleven_multilingual_v2.
# ELEVENLABS_MODEL_ID=eleven_multilingual_v2
# Production refuses ELEVENLABS_API_KEY without this (A11-30): Read aloud stays off for learners
# until ElevenLabs gives its written approval for under-18s. Set it only once that approval
# exists, and record where it is filed (status.md). Local and preview builds don't need it, nor
# does a judge demo, which refuses it: there Read aloud is on with the key and the voice alone (a
# hackathon exception of 2026-10-24, made-up learners only).
# UF_ELEVENLABS_MINORS_APPROVED=1

# ── Mobile app (apps/native) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The web app's address, inlined into the app's bundle at build time: public by design, so a URL
# and never a key (the app holds no secrets but the learner's own session token). Unset, a
# development build uses http://localhost:3000, which only the iOS simulator can reach: use
# http://10.0.2.2:3000 on the Android emulator, or this computer's LAN address
# (http://192.168.x.y:3000) on a phone running the development build (docs/store/android-dev-build.md).
# A release build refuses anything but https.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_UF_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
# `1` only on the judges' build for the FNB hackathon demo (a hackathon exception, set in the EAS
# "preview" environment with EXPO_PUBLIC_UF_API_URL=https://universityflow.tumoolo.tech;
# docs/store/judges-app.md): the sign-in screen first says it is the demo, made-up details and a
# made-up 080 number. Words only: the demo's server is what refuses a cellphone and sends nothing.
# Unset on every other build. Public (inlined into the bundle), never a key.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_UF_DEMO=1
# The app's EAS project id (a UUID), read by apps/native/app.config.ts into `extra.eas.projectId`.
# Set it after `npx eas-cli@latest init` in apps/native, in your shell and in each EAS environment
# (docs/store/release-checklist.md section 1). Not a secret. Every EAS build (development, preview,
# production) refuses to start without it, or with anything but a UUID (A7-21); `expo start` and
# `eas init` don't need it. Walk-through: docs/store/android-dev-build.md.
# UF_EAS_PROJECT_ID=
# Set by apps/native/metro.config.js itself; never set it by hand. It tells expo-router to use its
# stub icon converter for NativeTabs on Android (the app has none), so the 944 KB Material Symbols
# font stays out of the Android export (A4-05; apps/native/scripts/check-export.mjs holds it).
# EXPO_ROUTER_DISABLE_NATIVE_TABS_MD=1
